        "description": "<img src='https://i.cbc.ca/ais/00295cbb-85fb-4d67-9aa4-6dddde8f7198,1767976578820/full/max/0/default.jpg?im=Crop%2Crect%3D%280%2C450%2C8640%2C4860%29%3BResize%3D%28620%29' alt='Man at podium' width='620' height='349' title='Quebec Premier Fran\u00e7ois Legault participates in a press conference with Montreal Mayor Soraya Martinez Ferrada, not pictured, in Montreal&apos;s City Hall, on Friday, November 21, 2025. THE CANADIAN PRESS'/><p>It was a deal reached just in time for the holidays, averting the threat of multiple medical clinic closures and the departure of hundreds of doctors from the health system. But as the dust settles on the agreement, the initial relief is giving way to sharp questions about who actually stands to gain.\n</p>",
